Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 11, "type": "RSLT"}, {"questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n3le03ob05re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "id": 0}], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Problems I have found. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 12, "type": "DWS"}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": "", "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n3le03ob05re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"time": "100", "text": "<div class=\"center_text\"><strong>Data Validation Issues</div></strong>When users enter data into any data field of a program or app, the data validation rules try to identify the errors the users are making so that they can reduce their number. The amount of errors the system can identify depends on the validation rules the software developer sets when he develops the app.</br>\nAlthough it is a highly effective process, any time a user enters data manually, there is a slight chance that he makes an error. If a person misreads what is there on the source document or mishears what other person is telling him, this kind of errors surely occur. These errors also happen when a person rushes and is not careful when typing in the information. </br></br>", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0}, {"time": "44000", "text": "Many transcription errors also happen when people enter data in the form of long codes, like, numbers or letters that does not have any special meaning to the user. An example of this kind of error might be entering \u201cKile\u201d instead of \u201cKyle.\u201d </br>\nThere are also transposition errors. These kind of errors occur when the person entering the data changes by accident the order of numbers and letters. For example, typing a 96 instead of a 69. </br></br>", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 1}, {"time": "75500", "text": "There are some good methods to avoid this kind of errors. The easiest way to avoid them would be to double-check whatever you enter into a system. You can also enter the data twice, check it on the screen against the original paper document, or you may print out a copy of the data and compare the printout to the original paper document. </br>\nMost apps, programs, and systems use data validation tools to guarantee that the data in a database or system contains as few mistakes as possible when the users enter data into the program; avoiding this way any possible validation issues.", "image": "enpe7n3le03ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 2}], "audiosrc": "enpe7n3le03ob05re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar"}]}